# Line endings.
#
# The repo is built and run on Linux (WSL2), so the working tree is LF
# everywhere, on every platform. This is deliberate rather than the usual
# `text=auto`: a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true would rewrite
# tools/render-canary.sh and testdata/make-fixtures.sh with CRLF, and a
# CRLF shebang line fails with a bare "bad interpreter" the moment that
# checkout is opened from WSL. Nothing in the toolchain -- gcc, CMake,
# Ninja, Qt's qmlcachegen, MSVC -- minds LF on Windows.
*               text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell is the exception: these two run on the Windows side, and CRLF
# is what that platform's tooling expects.
*.ps1           text eol=crlf

# Subtitle fixtures. LF is already implied above, but these are parsed
# byte-for-byte by the extraction tests, so pin them where they are visible.
*.srt           text eol=lf
*.ass           text eol=lf

# The conformance corpus is exempt from all of the above, and the exemption is
# load-bearing rather than tidy-minded. Those files are committed as bytes so
# that every platform decodes identical input, and several of them encode a
# specific byte sequence on purpose -- src/basic.en.srt carries CRLF to pin how
# the parser handles it. Under the `*.srt text eol=lf` rule one line above, git
# would normalise that to LF on commit and the case would silently stop testing
# anything, while still passing. `-text` disables normalisation entirely.
testdata/conformance/**  -text

# Media and other binaries: never diff, never touch the bytes. Most of these
# are generated and gitignored, but the marker has to exist for the cases
# where one is committed on purpose (icons, a captured frame in a bug report).
*.mp4           binary
*.mkv           binary
*.mka           binary
*.webm          binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.ico           binary
*.gif           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.ttf           binary
*.otf           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary

# SVG is text, and worth diffing -- trap 23 was a one-character XML error.
*.svg           text eol=lf diff
